  "_shipping": {
    "vqa_zero_shot_fit": 20.0,
    "change_qa_zero_shot_fit": 20.0,
    "decision": "The deployed zero-shot scorer's softmax confidence is poorly calibrated and near-uninformative on foreign benchmarks (see confidence_auroc and the ceiling-pinned T): a single scalar can only reduce ECE by collapsing confidence toward the 0.5 fixed point, so the fit degenerates rather than yielding a usable temperature. The shipped pipeline therefore does NOT expose raw scorer softmax as answer confidence -- it grounds confidence in auditable spectral fractions + cross-model reconciliation (stage2/heads.py). integrate.DEFAULT_TEMPERATURES retains conservative priors for the grounded heads, documented as design-calibrated rather than benchmark-fit. Where confidence IS informative (task-adapted scorers, the mission-corpus deployment setting), temperature scaling gives a sensible non-degenerate T and a real ECE reduction -- see results['supervised']."
  }
